NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY ASSETS

The MIT license above covers this project's own source code
(index.js, client.js, lib/, helper/).

It does NOT cover the artwork and engine under assets/emotion-ball/.
Those files come from the "Emotion Ball" project and remain under the
"Emotion Ball Community License" (see assets/emotion-ball/LICENSE and
assets/emotion-ball/NOTICE.md):

  - the ball character's visual design (body, colors, ribbon FX) is for
    personal study only — commercial use is prohibited and no commercial
    license will ever be offered for it;
  - the engine source and emotion configuration data are free for
    non-commercial use; commercial licensing is separate.

If you want to use this plugin commercially, replace assets/emotion-ball/
with your own artwork (the renderer only needs ball.html + js/).
